          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7.2.1 Experimental Probability: Performing Observations or Experiments"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.159,
            0.885,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Another way of obtaining objective estimates for probabilities is to perform an experiment. In an experiment, the event is a result of the experiment and is called an "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "outcome",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". The set of all possible outcomes in an experiment is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "sample space",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.237,
            0.885,
            0.276
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The sample space may be listed within brackets, separated by commas as shown below."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.28,
            0.596,
            0.3
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Experiment: A coin is tossed"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.3,
            0.737,
            0.32
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Possible Outcomes: Heads (H) or Tails (T) (See Fig. 7.2)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.32,
            0.382,
            0.34
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Sample Space: {H, T}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.346,
            0.446,
            0.366
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Experiment: A die is rolled"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.366,
            0.884,
            0.405
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Possible Outcomes: The top side of the die shows 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, or 6 dots (See Fig. 7.3)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.405,
            0.471,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Sample Space: {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.311,
            0.43,
            0.485,
            0.58
          ],
          "content": [
            {
